	(text "Shows song and part, e.g. 03.2 (the decimal point after digit 2).\nU6 is the chip on the breadboard's Adafruit backpack (product 878), so the\nbreadboard firmware drives it unchanged: ROW0-7 = segments A-G and DP,\nCOM0, COM1, COM3, COM4 = digits 1-4.  U6 limits the segment current itself,\nso there are no resistors; brightness is set in firmware (16 steps).\nRuns from 3.3V so its I2C pins match the RP2040.  Fixed I2C address 0x70.\nDS1 is a 0.56-inch red display, the same size as the breadboard's."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 154.94 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "6dace2eb-37c9-4bf4-bb03-098d38e6a4ac")
	)
